# Everything the image does not need, kept out of the build context.
#
# target/ matters most: after a local `sbt assembly` it holds a 132MB jar plus the whole compiled
# tree, all of which would be uploaded to the daemon on every build and then thrown away, since the
# build stage produces its own.
target/
modules/*/target/
project/target/
project/project/
.bloop/
.bsp/
.metals/
.scala-build/

.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/

# Never let a real .env reach an image layer -- it holds the Authlete service access token and the
# interaction shared secret. Configuration is injected at run time.
.env
*.env
!.env.example

*.md
Makefile
.gitignore
.scalafmt.conf.bak
